type: software
title: "Displacement Observatory"
abstract: >-
  Register, trade panel, estimators, tests and decision log for testing whether EU restrictions on pesticides
  relocate trade to unrestricted destinations, and the arithmetic showing that public HS6 trade data cannot
  answer that question at the level of a single substance.
authors:
  - given-names: "Aya"
    # PLACEHOLDER, not a real value: family-names is a required sub-field once given-names is used, so this
    # string stands in for it. It is schema-valid (family-names has no format constraint) but not a name.
    # Replace with the real family name before publishing; do not invent one.
    family-names: "TBD-FAMILY-NAME-PENDING"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
# repository-code intentionally omitted (it is optional in the CFF schema): no placeholder string satisfies
# the schema's URI pattern (a bare "REPLACE-ME"-style value fails cffconvert's validator), and inventing a
# real-looking URL risks being mistaken for one. Add it, as a genuine https URL, once the repo is pushed.
keywords:
  - trade
  - pesticides
  - regulatory displacement
  - statistical power
  - difference-in-differences
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: "Public HS6 trade data cannot answer substance-level displacement questions: a detection-threshold analysis of EU pesticide restrictions"
